IME it's not _too_ unusual for something in the zoo to manage to
pick up the AoR before I reach it. What was _really_ annoying was
the time that happened and also there was another unidentified
amulet lying around the zoo, so I couldn't tell _which_ was the AoR
and I was absolutely sure the other one would turn out to be a
cursed AoStrangulation.

So I kept both and waited to find an altar or make a pet, only a
dwarf showed up at long range with a wand of magic missile and I
decided to risk putting one of them on. What do you know, it _was_
the wrong one and the wrong one _was_ a cursed AoStrangulation.
Sigh. Get holy water out of BoH, dip amulet, remove amulet, put
right amulet on, dwarf by this time has emptied the entire wand into
me and reached melee range so I kill him the old-fashioned way with
a few HP to spare. In retrospect I should have stuck with the plan
of lugging both amulets to the next altar; I could probably have had
the dwarf dead by thrown daggers three turns earlier if I hadn't
wasted time amulet-shuffling.
